"""Mutations of the animation actor (src/game/animation_actor.cpp, part 6b) for ../mutfast.py with the
actors build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_animation.py --models DIR --build build_item.bat --check check_item.py

Each should make check_item.py fail (or the harness crash / hang). Left out as equivalent: the
creator's Destroy (memory only), the property table (read by nothing), the NaN branches of Hit and of
the box radius's largest scale, the unused centre w, the constructor's ReleaseModel (on an empty
actor it only zeroes the damage, which the member initialiser already does), AddCollision's null test (CreateCollisions stops at the
first missing frame), the note's second terminator (sscanf's %f stops at the space), Finish's
DeleteCollisions (CreateCollisions deletes them first, with or without the copy), LoadGame's Stop(false)
against Stop(true) (loading silences all the flag controls).

Results (2026-10-25): the first run of 300 caught 272 (15 by a crash or a timeout); of the 28 survivors 5
were equivalent (dropped, above), "load failed id" now maps to a state chunk, and 22 needed new cases
(an unparsable and a near-miss "matid", a non-model owner, a flat box, point / unit / empty boxes, x-
and y-largest world scales, z moves of a wing, a gunner in a non-car vehicle, a non-unit frame scale,
StopMission on a standing actor, the default material's armour, an empty collision frame name, Stop
without a frame, the destroy path's message bit, WriteState after the animation, the load refresh,
the hit points' -1 floor). The rerun: all 295 caught."""
